"engenn5le08ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": " The First Conditional ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You can use the first conditional to talk about actions and situations in the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "There are two parts to the sentence. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "One part is the <span class =\"strong\">condition</span>. The other part is the <span class =\"strong\">result</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Form:<br /><span class=\"italic\"> If + subject + Simple Present tense  + subject + will/won't</span><br /> You use a comma after the condition in this form. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can flip the two parts of the sentence so that the result comes first. It can be in interrogative form. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Form:<br /><span class=\"italic\"> Will/Won't + subject + if + subject + Simple Present tense  ?</span><br/><br/> You can also use the future time clauses <span class=\"italic\">when</span> and  <span class=\"italic\">after</span> in the condition.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\"> Condition </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\">Result</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">After it rains, </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> we will go inside. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> If we leave at 4 p.m. sharp,</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">we'll get to the camp by 9 p.m.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "&nbsp;", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\">Result </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\">Condition</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> Will we visit the museum </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> when we have time? </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> We will make pit stops along the way</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> if the weather isn't too bad.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": " Quantifiers ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use a quantifier before a noun to indicate the amount or number of an item.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use quantifiers with both count and non-count nouns.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use all of the quantifiers below with both count and non-count nouns.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\"> Quantifier </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\">Meaning</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"more<br /> less/fewer<br /> no/none<br /> any /not any<br /> some<br /> a lot of / lots of<br /> plenty of<br /> enough\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a larger number/amount<br /> a smaller number/amount<br /> zero<br /> ask about a number or amount/say there is no<br /> a small number/amount<br /> a very large number/amount<br /> more than you need<br /> as much as you need\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I hope there's no rain tomorrow.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We've had plenty of rain this whole week!", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "nature reserve", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an area of land where wild animals and plants are protected  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We can go to the nature reserve.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le08ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about things to do on a trip.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "double-decker bus", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a bus with two levels ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We are taking a tour of the city on the double-decker bus.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le08ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Sweet!", "type": "name"}, {"content": "great; excellent", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sweet. I hope we can go tomorrow.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le08ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "museum ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a building where important objects are kept and open to the public ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I want to go to the city museum.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le08ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "hike", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a long walk in the mountains", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The safari includes a hike to the mountains.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le08ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "bus ride", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a journey in a bus", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The bus ride is five hours long.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le08ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "pit stop", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a stop when driving on a long journey", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Are we making a pit stop here?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le08ob10aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Read the sample chain poem below: <br/>Sample:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">If I drink lots of coffee,<br/>I'll stay awake tonight.<br/> If I stay awake tonight,<br/> I will fall asleep in the morning.<br/> And if I fall asleep in the morning,<br/> My teacher will be angry.<br/></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Think of a something that could happen to you. Write it down.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Think of a result that will happen because of that.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Keep going.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write 6 \u201cchains\u201d.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read out your chain poem to a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Listen to their poem.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I write 6 lines.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use the first conditional.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use a quantifier.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read my poem aloud.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I listen to a poem.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "engenn5le08ob10re2aud01", "images": [{"image": "engenn5le08ob10re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "time": "0", "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn5le08ob10re2img01.jpg", "id": 1, "time": "100", "text": "<span class =\"strong\">Tour Guide</span>: If it rains tomorrow, we won't be boarding the hot-air balloon.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Tourist</span>: What will we do then?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Tour Guide</span>: Well, there's several things to do. We can take a tour of the city or a nature reserve.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Tourist</span>: A city tour? Will we take a double-decker bus, if we go on that tour?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Tour Guide</span>: Definitely.<br/>\n<span class =\"strong\">Tourist</span>: Sweet. I'd like to do that."}, {"image": "engenn5le08ob10re2img08.jpg", "id": 2, "time": "20500", "text": "<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: What other things can we do?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Tour Guide</span>: We can visit some of the museums in Windhoek or go on a hike.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: That sounds tiring!<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Tour Guide</span>: If it continues raining tomorrow, we'll be taking a bus to Sossusvlei Wilderness Camp in the afternoon."}, {"image": "engenn5le08ob10re2img06.jpg", "id": 3, "time": "35000", "text": "<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: How long will that take?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Tour Guide</span>: If we leave at 4 p.m. sharp, we'll get to the camp by 9 p.m.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Tourist</span>: A five hour bus ride?! Any pit stops?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Tour Guide</span>: We will make pit stops along the way, if the weather isn't too bad."}], "coverimg": "engenn5le08ob10re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "I can talk about travel and things to do on a trip. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can talk about hypothetical actions and ev